<!--
Declares a deliberately non-default instance.

ThermalManagerService waits for IThermal/default and blocks while it does, so
declaring that name commits the system server to a service that may not start,
which is how the earlier ODM attempt hung between the boot trigger and
boot-completed. servicemanager, meanwhile, refuses to register any VINTF HAL
under a name it cannot find declared.

An extra instance satisfies servicemanager without the framework ever waiting
for it, so the provider can be started and queried directly. Only once it
answers does the instance become default.
-->
<manifest version="2.0" type="framework">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.thermal</name>
        <version>2</version>
        <fqname>IThermal/odinprobe</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
